a love that will not just vanish because God just doesn't feel it anymore.

00:44:35.300 --> 00:44:37.460
He is committed to this and it costs him something,

00:44:37.760 --> 00:44:41.260
and that is the radical grace that he calls us to show one another as well.

00:44:43.860 --> 00:44:48.620
For us, we view our life group communities as something to commit to.

00:44:51.420 --> 00:44:56.280
Not to say like you're signing a contract and like you have to show up to X amount of dates.

00:44:56.380 --> 00:44:57.420
That's not it at all.

00:44:57.480 --> 00:44:58.780
It is a relational thing.

00:44:58.860 --> 00:45:00.120
And it's saying, hey, I'm joining this group.

00:45:00.360 --> 00:45:02.600
And sure, I may have weeks where I can't come

00:45:02.600 --> 00:45:04.900
and I can't make the weekly meeting or whatever else.

00:45:04.940 --> 00:45:05.840
But still, these are my people.

00:45:05.920 --> 00:45:07.040
These are my relationships.

00:45:07.220 --> 00:45:09.580
These are my community for this year.

00:45:09.860 --> 00:45:11.500
These are the people that I want to be connected to

00:45:11.500 --> 00:45:13.020
in love and grace because of Jesus.

00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:16.380
What prevents that commitment?

00:45:20.990 --> 00:45:23.410
I mean, there's superficial stuff.

00:45:24.890 --> 00:45:26.590
Sickness can keep you from people.

00:45:27.510 --> 00:45:29.050
If some of you are prone to being sick,

00:45:29.050 --> 00:45:32.990
I get sick every other day

00:45:32.990 --> 00:45:34.510
please don't talk to me

00:45:34.510 --> 00:45:35.630
because I don't want to get you sick

00:45:35.630 --> 00:45:36.950
I mean that might be a thing

00:45:36.950 --> 00:45:39.490
hopefully your life groups care about you enough

00:45:39.490 --> 00:45:40.490
to bring you care packages

00:45:40.490 --> 00:45:43.210
and medicine and soups

00:45:43.210 --> 00:45:43.750
and all that

00:45:43.750 --> 00:45:47.470
but honestly most of it tends to be

00:45:47.470 --> 00:45:47.990
fear

00:45:47.990 --> 00:45:51.660
I know I'm going to date myself

00:45:51.660 --> 00:45:53.880
and show myself as old

00:45:53.880 --> 00:45:58.140
there's an old phrase that I can't get over

00:45:58.140 --> 00:46:00.880
that for some of us

00:46:00.880 --> 00:46:03.500
what's going to challenge our commitment

00:46:03.500 --> 00:46:05.540
to these communities to find this grace

00:46:05.540 --> 00:46:07.420
is the fear of missing out.

00:46:09.620 --> 00:46:10.860
FOMO is no longer a thing, right?

00:46:11.360 --> 00:46:13.120
You guys don't say that on a day-to-day basis.

00:46:14.380 --> 00:46:15.220
Sinka, do you say that ever?

00:46:16.180 --> 00:46:16.660
Is it a thing?

00:46:16.980 --> 00:46:17.740
You guys still say FOMO?

00:46:18.500 --> 00:46:19.940
Yes, I'm not too old, yes.

00:46:20.420 --> 00:46:22.460
All right, FOMO, fear of missing out.

00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:25.160
What causes someone to say,

00:46:25.260 --> 00:46:26.500
I don't want to commit to you,

00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:28.620
I think I have better options.

00:46:28.620 --> 00:46:35.860
i have a better option for fun i have a better option for my future success i have a better

00:46:35.860 --> 00:46:39.480
option for my career and i'm not saying that these things are not important or valuable

00:46:39.480 --> 00:46:44.180
but when we are driven by that fear when we're driven by a fear of saying i want i am worried

00:46:44.180 --> 00:46:49.120
that there's something better out there for me then we look at our relationships and say you're

00:46:49.120 --> 00:46:54.140
not a relationship you're a commodity you're something for me to consume you're something

00:46:54.140 --> 00:46:58.440
that if you don't meet up to my standards if you don't meet up to my desires then what good are you

00:46:58.440 --> 00:47:07.260
I'm out. Jesus didn't do that with us. It cost him something to show us love. It cost him something

00:47:07.260 --> 00:47:12.380
to build that relationship with us. And for us to say we want our life groups to show Christ's love

00:47:12.380 --> 00:47:17.420
means that we are going to commit to one another. Again, yes, there are seasons where we are more

00:47:17.420 --> 00:47:21.900
active, less active. I mean, those things happen. But for us to relationally say, this is the people

00:47:21.900 --> 00:47:29.100
that God has called me to commit to so that I can both experience and show God's radical grace.

00:47:32.860 --> 00:47:35.360
And finally, the last principle coming from chapter 2, verse 1.

00:47:35.860 --> 00:47:38.960
Radical grace enables us to be open to being hurt.

00:47:41.080 --> 00:47:41.840
2-1.

00:47:42.380 --> 00:47:48.120
So put away all malice, all deceit, hypocrisy, and envy, and slander.

00:47:48.820 --> 00:47:49.380
All slander.

00:47:52.110 --> 00:47:58.900
If you look at that list, malice, deceit, lying, hypocrisy,

00:47:59.800 --> 00:48:01.100
when you're envious or jealous,

00:48:01.100 --> 00:48:03.680
when you start slandering all the people, talking bad about them,

00:48:03.680 --> 00:48:07.100
trying to destroy their reputations.

00:48:07.220 --> 00:48:08.160
Where does that come from?

00:48:09.580 --> 00:48:10.920
Honestly, I look at that list

00:48:10.920 --> 00:48:14.020
and I'm thinking, man, the people who do this

00:48:14.020 --> 00:48:15.720
are people who have been hurt

00:48:15.720 --> 00:48:17.840
and they don't want to be hurt again.

00:48:21.830 --> 00:48:24.430
Hurt people, slander others.

00:48:24.570 --> 00:48:28.030
Hurt people, lie.

00:48:28.890 --> 00:48:29.910
And I'm going to get what I want.

00:48:29.950 --> 00:48:31.110
I'm going to lie to get what I want

00:48:31.110 --> 00:48:32.970
because I've been hurt and disappointed before.

00:48:35.730 --> 00:48:36.410
Radical grace.

00:48:36.410 --> 00:48:38.890
If we truly understand Christ's radical grace

00:48:38.890 --> 00:48:40.910
and how he wants us to live that on the community.

00:48:41.550 --> 00:48:43.130
It means that, man, we have to be vulnerable,

00:48:43.290 --> 00:48:43.950
we have to be open,

00:48:44.050 --> 00:48:45.850
we have to be willing to say,

00:48:45.950 --> 00:48:48.210
I'm going to expose myself to these people

00:48:48.210 --> 00:48:49.990
as a sign of commitment to them,

00:48:50.230 --> 00:48:51.910
as a sign of grace for them,

00:48:52.030 --> 00:48:54.890
and also to be exposed so that I can receive grace.

00:48:54.970 --> 00:48:56.910
Because I don't know about you,

00:48:57.050 --> 00:48:58.570
there's a couple of situations

00:48:58.570 --> 00:49:00.730
where being vulnerable really matter.

00:49:00.830 --> 00:49:01.870
If you are in a battle

00:49:01.870 --> 00:49:03.490
and you are exposed with no armor,

00:49:03.610 --> 00:49:06.310
you are opening yourself up to being hurt for sure.

00:49:07.510 --> 00:49:08.430
But at the same time,

00:49:08.430 --> 00:49:12.970
I imagine if you're in a hospital and you need to get a surgery, you are exposing yourself.

00:49:13.070 --> 00:49:13.770
You're stripped naked.

00:49:14.110 --> 00:49:18.510
The team is looking at your body and trying to explore where this pain or this issue is coming from.

00:49:18.670 --> 00:49:22.230
You are exposing yourself to be hurt, but you're not experiencing that hurt in the hospital.

00:49:22.330 --> 00:49:25.130
You're experiencing people going into your life, going deep and saying,

00:49:25.290 --> 00:49:26.690
this is where I want your healing to be found.

00:49:29.980 --> 00:49:34.020
Radical grace, if we understand it, it enables us to be open to being hurt.

00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:36.480
And yes, we might get hurt.

00:49:37.080 --> 00:49:40.040
Vulnerability, there is that risk that runs from there.

00:49:41.700 --> 00:49:43.460
But it's saying, if I'm open to being hurt,

00:49:43.560 --> 00:49:45.420
hopefully that'll help others find

00:49:45.420 --> 00:49:47.460
grace. Maybe as

00:49:47.460 --> 00:49:49.300
I'm being vulnerable, people will

00:49:49.300 --> 00:49:51.340
also feel like they can be vulnerable and

00:49:51.340 --> 00:49:53.360
find the deeper healing that they need to find

00:49:53.360 --> 00:49:57.790
in Jesus Christ. Because here's

00:49:57.790 --> 00:49:59.910
the truth. Vulnerability, I mean, God knows

00:49:59.910 --> 00:50:01.770
everything about you. He knows the worst

00:50:01.770 --> 00:50:03.070
things about you.

00:50:04.230 --> 00:50:05.990
He's already known that. He's already

00:50:05.990 --> 00:50:07.990
loved you. And for us,

00:50:08.010 --> 00:50:09.930
as we want to explore that in community, we want

00:50:09.930 --> 00:50:11.870
to say, if God loves us at our worst,

00:50:11.870 --> 00:50:13.690
we want to be free to show that to others

00:50:13.690 --> 00:50:15.950
to have people

00:50:15.950 --> 00:50:17.750
speak love and grace back into our lives

00:50:17.750 --> 00:50:19.410
and to be able to share that with others as well

00:50:19.410 --> 00:50:28.580
I hope for every single one of us

00:50:28.580 --> 00:50:30.420
that we experience

00:50:30.420 --> 00:50:32.260
Jesus' radical grace that he

00:50:32.260 --> 00:50:32.580
shows

00:50:32.580 --> 00:50:36.060
but I also hope that we understand

00:50:36.060 --> 00:50:37.940
that he calls us to join him

00:50:37.940 --> 00:50:40.260
saying the radical grace that I'm showing

00:50:40.260 --> 00:50:42.180
to you, I want this

00:50:42.180 --> 00:50:44.200
to be lived out in your life groups or whatever

00:50:44.200 --> 00:50:46.220
communities that you commit to this

00:50:46.220 --> 00:50:48.120
year. That's why the one thing

00:50:48.120 --> 00:50:49.860
for today is this, is to commit to biblical

00:50:49.860 --> 00:50:52.060
community, to find and

00:50:52.060 --> 00:50:53.920
to demonstrate radical

00:50:53.920 --> 00:50:58.430
grace. Whether it's here or

00:50:58.430 --> 00:51:00.270
elsewhere, I hope that happens for us.

00:51:02.230 --> 00:51:04.450
It's pretty easy to find

00:51:04.450 --> 00:51:05.750
a Bible study if you want to.

00:51:06.430 --> 00:51:08.250
Hey, we're just here to study a passage.

00:51:09.430 --> 00:51:10.550
It's pretty easy to find

00:51:10.550 --> 00:51:12.570
a friend group if you have the right hobbies

00:51:12.570 --> 00:51:14.490
or if you have the right interest or the personality

00:51:14.490 --> 00:51:16.770
or ethnic background or something like that.

00:51:19.180 --> 00:51:19.880
But to find

00:51:19.880 --> 00:51:21.800
communities where we can

00:51:21.800 --> 00:51:23.720
experience this radical grace, it does

00:51:23.720 --> 00:51:25.080
take a bit of commitment for us.

00:51:26.280 --> 00:51:27.820
But it's possible

00:51:27.820 --> 00:51:29.880
because Jesus has already

00:51:29.880 --> 00:51:30.820
shown it to us as well.
